.TH QUADCAP 1 "2026" "quadcap" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quadcap \- record a games console through an Elgato 4K60 Pro MK.2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadcap
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadcap
opens a window showing the console attached to the capture card and records it
while the card passes the picture through to a monitor untouched.
.PP
The preview is uploaded to the GPU and shown at capture rate. A rolling
flashback buffer is kept on disk, so the last few minutes can be written out
after something worth keeping has already happened. Recordings carry the game
audio and the microphone as separate tracks alongside a mixed one, and the
mixer in the window sets the levels of the mixed track only, leaving the
isolated tracks raw.
.PP
Only one instance runs at a time: the sound device is opened exclusively, so a
second copy would take the audio away from the first. Starting quadcap again
raises the window that is already open.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Videos/quadcap
Recordings and saved flashback clips.
.TP
.I /usr/share/quadcap/install.sh
Installs the sc0710 kernel module through DKMS, signing it for Secure Boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadcapd (1)
